// of every row in [B, S], returned as values plus int64 column indices.
//
// Radix selection on the order-preserving uint32 view of the float. The key is
// resolved digit by digit, so no comparison sort is needed:
//
//   scores --[hist]--> per-row histogram of the top 11 key bits
//              |
//              +--[gather]--> highest 11-bit digit D that still leaves room:
//              |              digit > D  => selected (written straight out)
//              |              digit == D => candidate (compacted, key + index)
//              |
//              +--[finalize]--> two more radix levels over the candidates only,
//                               resolving the exact K-th key.
//
//   key(bits) = bits "'^ (bits >> 31 ? ~0 : 0x80000000)   // -inf .. +inf ascending
//
// Each block histograms its share of the row in shared memory; one atomic round
// folds the block histograms into the row histogram. The cut digit follows from
// the suffix sums of that histogram, recomputed by every block (8 KB, L2 warm).
